    "body": "**Hand check of `camcraft-ui-709` (head 47a33610) by the user, 2026-11-10.** Picking follows the one rule: whole welded faces (the bore face picks as one face), whole feature-edge chains (a 137 mm open chain, a 25 mm straight edge), corner points, and no tessellation seams.\n\n**One bug:** in the Setups page's **+Y / +X by Two points**, only the **first** picked point stays drawn (purple marker) after the second is picked, although the page reads \"2 points on 'Milling-test' (…) -> (…)\". The second point's marker disappears. It looks like the axis-draft overlay draws only the first vertex of a two-point pick, possibly the feature-line drawing for vertex picks in `selection_feature_lines` / `feature_lines`. Please pin it with a test that both points draw after the second pick.\n\n**Not a bug** (the user asked how to apply): Apply axes stays greyed while both +X and +Y hold the same two points reversed (\"picks are parallel\"), which is correct. With one axis picked it enables (\"turns the part 90° about Z\").",
