    "body": "Hand-check bug fixed in e5d3b32e: only the first of two picked points stayed marked.\n\n**Cause.** Both points were always picked and resolved, and both 3D crosses were in the overlay buffer; I checked this on Milling-test.step. But each cross is tiny: its arm hits the 0.5 mm floor, so the whole cross is about 3 px of 1 px lines. It is also depth-tested and half buried in the faces and edges it marks. So whether a corner showed came down to depth and z-fighting at that corner.\n\n**Fix.** Every picked point now also gets a ~5 px screen-space violet diamond, the same shape as the hover marker, drawn with a 2 px stroke and never depth-tested.\n- `interact::shown_picks` is the one pick list the overlay draws.\n- `vertex_pick::picked_point_marks` builds the marks.\n- `shell.rs` paints them under the yellow hover.\n\n**Pinned by** `two_point_marks::both_points_of_a_two_point_axis_stay_marked_on_the_users_part`. It runs on Milling-test.step with real clicks and asserts one screen mark per pick, centred on its point. It fails with the marks stubbed out. Also added: `setup_axis_tests::both_picked_points_keep_their_markers` and `one_pick_rule::both_clicked_points_of_an_axis_keep_their_markers`.\n\n**Gate:**\n- ui all suites green (lib 448).\n- app lib 107, `axis_align` 10, `feature_pick` 7, `feature_pick_wire` 4, `pick` 9, `points_align` 8.\n- clippy `-D warnings` clean.\n\n**Note on #746:** it paints 6 px filled discs for align picks. Whichever lands second keeps one marker style.\n\nStill a draft for the re-check. `~/camcraft-builds/camcraft-ui-709` is being rebuilt from e5d3b32e.",
